  "publicationDraft": "Stilly spent five FAAB to insure Aaron Jones with his Green Bay understudy. Dillon was a reserve when acquired, but Jones’ November knee injury turned the insurance policy into a usable starter. Naturally, Dillon’s 26.80-point breakout happened on Stilly’s bench. He started the following week for 12.70 and eventually contributed 54.40 across five observed starts, including 7.10 in an unpaired Week 16 lineup. Mitch sold a bench back for waiver flexibility; the exact benefit of those five dollars cannot be isolated without a budget ledger. Stilly bought meaningful depth without surrendering a player. Not a franchise-altering heist, just a damn sensible purchase.",
